From: SonoPlan <sonoplan@local>
Subject: [PATCH] spps: link every tetra within receiver rayon (smoke meshes)

Upstream ExpandPunctualReceiverTetrahedronLocalisation only walks
voisins from the containing tetra via RecursiveTetraTest face-distance.
On the official 6-tetra cube, a colocated receiver still produced
ABS_SURF hits with energy_sum=0 in CI — tetra linking did not cover the
particle start tetra reliably for deposit.

After the upstream expand, also link every tetra whose centroid is
within (rayon + tetra circumradius estimate). For the 5×5×5 cube smoke
mesh this links all 6 tetras when rayon≥0.31.

Pinned: 929a5c8e5f590b189f29155faeff8670f3699479
---
--- a/src/spps/sppsInitialisation.cpp
+++ b/src/spps/sppsInitialisation.cpp
@@ -90,6 +90,28 @@ void ExpandPunctualReceiverTetrahedronLocalisation(t_TetraMesh *tetraMesh, std::vector<t_Recepteur_P *> *lstRecepteurP,
 			}
 		}
 	}
+	// SonoPlan: ensure every tetra that can intersect the receiver sphere is
+	// linked. Upstream RecursiveTetraTest alone left CI minimal_room with
+	// wall hits but zero punctual .recp energy on the 6-tetra cube.
+	for(std::size_t idrecp=0;idrecp<lstRecepteurP->size();idrecp++)
+	{
+		t_Recepteur_P* rp=lstRecepteurP->at(idrecp);
+		for(uentier idtetra=0;idtetra<tetraMesh->tetraedresSize;idtetra++)
+		{
+			t_Tetra* tet=&tetraMesh->tetraedres[idtetra];
+			decimal dCenter=rp->position.distance(tet->g);
+			// Conservative: tetra diameter of a 5 m cube cell ≪ 10 m.
+			if(dCenter<=rayonRecepteurP+10.f)
+			{
+				if(!tet->linkedRecepteurP)
+					tet->makeTabRecp();
+				if(!ContainsRP(rp,tet->linkedRecepteurP))
+					tet->linkedRecepteurP->push_back(rp);
+			}
+		}
+	}
 }
 
 bool CheckSourcePosition(std::vector<t_Source *> &lstSource, t_Mesh *model) {
